  "reasoning": "*   Role: Content policy analyst.\n    *   Context: \"Friends\" app (User pays Expert).\n    *   Goal: Find violations in three categories: `PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, `Explicit-Flirting`.\n    *   Output: Minified JSON object following a specific schema.\n    *   Constraints:\n        *   Ignore \"Allowed\" items (greetings, small talk, personal details without contact info, etc.).\n        *   Handle \"About a Violation\" (warnings, stories, refusals, etc.) as `violation: \"no\"` and `c <= 0.3`.\n        *   Categories must be exactly: `PlatformMove`, `SuspiciousActivity`, `Explicit-Flirting`.\n        *   Confidence scale: 0.9 (strong), 0.6 (weaker), 0.3 (about/partial), 0.1 (probably not).\n\n    *   [00:00] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:03] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:05] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:06] Will you show your face? (Request to show face. Is this `Explicit-Flirting`? The policy says \"Show or open when it is about the body or the video\". However, \"show your face\" is generally considered a normal request in a video/audio call app to see who they are talking to, unless it's explicitly sexual. In the context of \"Friends\" app, asking to see the face is usually not a violation unless it's \"show me your [body part]\". Let's check the \"Allowed\" section: \"Show or open about things that are not the body: 'Show me your city', 'Open the app', 'Show me dancing'\". Face is generally not considered \"nudity\" or \"sexual talk\". It's a basic request for identity/presence. I will treat this as ordinary conversation/allowed.)\n    *   [00:11] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:14] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:17] Hello. (Greeting - Allowed)\n    *   [00:20] Hi, where are you from? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:22] I am from Delhi. (Personal detail - Allowed)\n    *   [00:26] Where in Delhi? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:28] Gurgaon. (Personal detail - Allowed)\n    *   [00:31] Where? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:33] Gurgaon. (Personal detail - Allowed)\n    *   [00:35] Is Gurgaon in Delhi? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:37] Then where is it? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:40] Gurgaon is a separate place. (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:43] It comes in that, right? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:44] It doesn't come in Delhi, Gurgaon. (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:46] Where do you live? (Small talk - Allowed)\n    *   [00:49] I live in Jaipur. (Personal detail - Allowed)\n    *   [00:51] Okay. (Filler - Allowed)\n    *   [00:53] Yes. (Filler - Allowed)\n    *   [00:56] What do you do? (Small talk - Allowed)\n\n    *   `PlatformMove`: No mention of other apps, phone numbers, or meeting in person.\n    *   `SuspiciousActivity`: No mention of money, rates, or payments for sexual services.\n    *   `Explicit-Flirting`: \"Will you show your face?\" is the only candidate. However, asking to see a face is not \"showing the body\" in a sexual sense, nor is it \"undressing\" or \"nudity\". It's a standard request in a call.\n\n    *   The conversation consists entirely of greetings, location questions, and basic introductions.\n    *   No violations found.\n\n    *   Return `{\"d\": []}`.",
